    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0558" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17388</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-09T18:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>State military commander informs me that 250 cavalry left Guzman 6 this morning
                    to intercept Villa and that other bodies are being moved north; also 350 cavalry
                    are being sent to Ojinaga. He expresses willingness to cooperate with the
                    Government of the United States in capture Villa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
